"This requires both presence of the dynamic tag ``DT_BIND_NOW``, and a "
"``GNU_RELRO`` program header."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.elf.elf.ELF.relro:6
msgid ""
"The `ELF Specification`_ describes how the linker should resolve symbols "
"immediately, as soon as a binary is loaded.  This can be emulated with "
"the ``LD_BIND_NOW=1`` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.elf.elf.ELF.relro:10
msgid "``DT_BIND_NOW``"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.elf.elf.ELF.relro:12
msgid ""
"If present in a shared object or executable, this entry instructs the "
"dynamic linker to process all relocations for the object containing this "
"entry before transferring control to the program. The presence of this "
"entry takes precedence over a directive to use lazy binding for this "
"object when specified through the environment or via ``dlopen(BA_LIB)``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.elf.elf.ELF.relro:19
msgid "(`page 81`_)"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.elf.elf.ELF.relro:21
msgid ""
"Separately, an extension to the GNU linker allows a binary to specify a "
"PT_GNU_RELRO_ program header, which describes the *region of memory which"
" is to be made read-only after relocations are complete.*"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.elf.elf.ELF.relro:25
msgid ""
"Finally, a new-ish extension which doesn't seem to have a canonical "
"source of documentation is DF_BIND_NOW_, which has supposedly superceded "
"``DT_BIND_NOW``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.elf.elf.ELF.relro:29
msgid "``DF_BIND_NOW``"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.elf.elf.ELF.relro:31
msgid ""
"If set in a shared object or executable, this flag instructs the dynamic "
"linker to process all relocations for the object containing this entry "
"before transferring control to the program. The presence of this entry "
"takes precedence over a directive to use lazy binding for this object "
"when specified through the environment or via ``dlopen(BA_LIB)``."
msgstr ""

